# C1 execution ledger

## Scope and rulings

- The principal architect selected the narrow invariant correction recorded in the B4b review package: only `core/pit_optimizer_v5/memory.py` may change.
- The authorized behavior is confined to `ExperimentRecordV5._validate_post_validation_identity`: an `exact_duplicate` whose policy revision equals its parent revision must validate an empty *actual* `validation.changed_symbols`; every other record must continue to match `template.changed_symbols`.
- B4b `runtime.py` and `artifacts.py` are held unchanged. B4c and all campaign activity are out of scope.
- The user explicitly prohibits tests, synthetic probes, model/API calls, credential access, evaluator/candidate evaluation, commits, pushes, deployment, and campaign restart/resume. These restrictions override generic development defaults.
- Verification is static only: scoped Ruff, in-memory compilation, narrow source/diff inspection, evaluator identity hashing, and read-only actual-artifact inspection.

