## Dependencies / consumer-producer notes

- `ExperimentIdentityV5` type and `ValidationResultV5` validity are checked before the changed-symbol comparison; subsequent existing identity validation and derivation still bind the policy-revision field after it.
- `StructuralTemplateV5.changed_symbols` remains the declared candidate change for all non-parent-identical records. The exception is conjunctive (`status == "exact_duplicate"` and parent-policy equality).
- Status evidence and post-validation identity derivation remain downstream of the corrected comparison and must not change.

## Completion boundary

The C1 package is ready for principal architect review. B4c is not started. The positive parent-identical exact-duplicate branch was not executed because the bounded real archive inventory contains no such record; it is documented as static review only.
